    "BRIEF_FACTS": "IN THE COURT OF HON\u2019BLE X ADDITIONAL JUNIOR CIVIL JUDGE- CUM- X ADDITIONAL METROPOLITAN MAGISTRATE, MEDCHAL MALKAJGIRI DISTRICT AT MEDCHAL\nHonoured Sir,\n            To-day i.e., on 01.11.2023 at 21:15 hrs received a petition from Through Telangana State Police Sri B. Venu Madhav, Sub Inspector of Police, Jawaharnagar Police Station, Rachakonda Commissionerate. Cell: 8712580052. In which reads as follows.\n\nThis is a Suo-moto case; Facts of the case are that the complainant Sri B. Venu Madhav, SIP stated that on 01.11.2023 at 17:00 hours, while he was conducting Vehicle Checking at Vikalangula Colony, Balajinagar, he found two persons suspiciously moving on Activa bike br.No TS08GE8903. On seeing the SI and staff, they tried to escape from the spot, however SI and staff caught the persons at 1715 hrs. Later SI and Staff searched the bike and found 250 gms of Dry Ganja in the dickey of the bike. Thereafter he informed the same to superior officers and secured two panchayathdars and briefed them to act as mediators. On enquiry they disclosed their names as 1) Tudumu Chitti Babu @ Chitti S/o Devaiah, age: 31 yrs, Occ: Painting, R/o; Santosh Nagar, Balajinagar, Kapra (M), Medchal (D). Cell: 8897459432, 2). Vagmari. Arjun S/o Nagappa, age: 35 yrs, Occ: Driver, Caste: SC-Madiga, R/o Near Indiramma Statue, Market Lane, Venkateshwara Balajinagar, Kapra Mandal, Medchal District. Cell: 9390561180. Then complainant recorded confession cum seizure panchanama in the presence of mediators in which they stated that today morning hours they purchased 250 gms of Ganja from Sonu, R/o; Balajinagar in order to sell the same to the needy persons and seized Dry Ganja 250 Grams and Activa Bike Br.No TS08GE8903 from the accused persons, affixed signed Panch chits on it. Hence complainant produced the accused persons in Jawaharnagar PS along with seized material and requested to take necessary action against them as per law. Hence the FIR.\n\n    /THE ORIGINAL DETAILED COMPLAINT IS ENCLOSED HERE WITH/\n     Received on 01.11.2023 at 21:15 hrs: - \n             As per the content of the above petition a case registered in Cr. No. 1161/2023 U/s 8(c) r/w 20 (b) (ii)(A) of NDPS Act and took up the investigation.\n \t\t\tSd/-\n                 (R. Laxman)\n           Sub-Inspector of Police,\n            PS: Jawahar Nagar,           \n      Rachakonda Commissionarate.\n  Copy Submitted W/Cs:\n 1). Through ACP Kushaiguda Division, Rachakonda Commissionerate. \n 2). The DCP, Malkajgiri Zone, Rachakonda Commissionerate &\n 3). The Commissioner of Police, Rachakonda Commissionerate for favour of             \n       Information.\n",
